                    {'heading': 'One loop, several jobs', 'body': 'You could loop once to total the scores and loop again to count passes — but one loop can do both. Keep two accumulators: total += s on every item, and passed += 1 only inside if s >= PASS_MARK. Each variable accumulates a different fact during the same pass over the data. This is how real data pipelines stay fast: one sweep through the data, collecting everything needed at once, instead of re-reading it for every question.'},
